From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:10:00 +0200
Subject: drm/panfrost: Gate the RK3399 GPU clocks in runtime suspend

The RK3399 Mali-T860 matches arm,mali-t860 and gets default_data, so
panfrost enables its clocks at probe and keeps them enabled until
unbind; runtime suspend powers the GPU off but leaves the clocks on.

On ROCK Pi 4A restore from hibernation hangs in genpd_restore_noirq()
of the GPU while panfrost is bound. With the clocks gated in runtime
suspend, as on the Allwinner H616 and the Renesas parts, it restores.

Match rockchip,rk3399-mali to default_pm_rt_data.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c
@@ -1172,6 +1172,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id dt_match[] = {
 	  .data = &amlogic_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "renesas,r9a08g046-mali", .data = &default_pm_rt_data },
 	{ .compatible = "renesas,r9a09g047-mali", .data = &default_pm_rt_data },
+	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rk3399-mali", .data = &default_pm_rt_data },
 	{ .compatible = "arm,mali-t604", .data = &default_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "arm,mali-t624", .data = &default_data, },
 	{ .compatible = "arm,mali-t628", .data = &default_data, },
--
